  "description": "BFe is our hardcore steel hardtail. Burly Intentions, Beautiful Ride. Long travel forks, big tyres, steep trails.\nSome bikes are fast. Some bikes are tough. The BFe is both, and it doesn't ask you to choose.\nThe Ride\nThis is Cotic's hardcore hardtail, built for longer travel forks, bigger terrain, and riders who want to point at something steep and commit. But here's the thing: despite the tough-sounding name and the aggressive intentions, the BFe has a beautiful ride feel. It is still a Cotic, after all. Forgiving, supple, springy, the signature steel character that defines every bike we build is fully present here, even in our most capable trail machine.\nThat makes it something rare. A hardtail that descends with complete confidence, climbs with ease, and pedals comfortably for hours.\nWhy Steel?\nThe BFe is built from our own Cotic Fm heat treated cromoly, with a reinforced Reynolds 853 down tube for maximum strength at minimum weight. It's tough enough for the hardest riding, and it still has the spring and give that makes a steel frame easier on you over a long day.\n\nKey details\n\nCotic Fm heat treated cromoly throughout, with a reinforced Reynolds 853 down tube. Maximum strength at minimum weight.\n44mm standard head tube for maximum steerer compatibility and durability.\nOvalform top tube to boost precision and maximise compliance.\nCotic exclusive design reinforced 35mm seat tube for massive pedalling stiffness and dropper seatpost compatibility.\nExternal dropper remote hose clips under the top tube, with stealth/internal seat tube dropper routing along the down tube.\nBridge-less S-bend chainstays with Cotic Hexten gussets for improved fatigue life and huge mud clearance: 29 x 2.6\" or 27.5 x 2.8\" rear tyres.\nISCG05 mount.\nUDH Double Decker Dropout: run either a 29\" or 27.5\" rear wheel with corrected geometry, frame angles and BB height stay identical either way.\nGeometry with commitment. Minimum 120mm travel forks, optimised around 140mm forks, maximum 160mm forks.\nLow slung design keeps the frame out of the way for those tight situations, and a long top tube/short stem setup lets you ride up to the trails without breaking your back.\nLoads of bottle bosses.\nFive sizes, C1 to C5, designed to be compact and chuckable.",
